<title>USA: U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.409 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.409 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 5-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 5-YEAR NOTES DUE SEPT 30, 2001</p>
<p>			     $12.502 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	6.409    Awarded At	99.856	6.375</p>
<p> MEDIAN    6.390    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 6.350    3 Percent	 NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.57 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 30.Sep.01</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    5-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 30.Sep.96</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 26.Sep.96</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  12.502 BLN USD		 CUSIP    912827Z54</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   32.178			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   477.00 MLN			  DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.375</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN   1.350			   PRICE	 99.856</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    6.350-6.409 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   6.409</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD DOWN FROM 6.568 PCT AT AUCTION ON 28.AUG.96</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD LOWEST SINCE 6.279 PCT AT AUCTION 24.APR.96</p>
